# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv

# Offline map tile cache (USGS National Map, public domain) - generated by install.py's optional
# download step on the target device, not something this repo ships or builds from source (unlike
# static/vendor/leaflet/, which IS committed - the library code itself, not the tile imagery).
# Renamed from osm_tiles/ 2026-09-14 when the source moved off OpenStreetMap, whose tile usage
# policy forbids exactly this kind of pre-download.
static/vendor/offline_tiles/
static/vendor/osm_tiles/

# Same class of thing as the OSM tile cache above - third-party tools install.py vendors onto
# the target device by cloning/downloading them at install time (ALEAPP/iLEAPP, UAC, pysim's
# source), never something this repo ships or builds from source.
/leapp/
/live_collection/
/pysim/

# Same class again - install.py builds mquire from source at install time
# and drops the resulting binary here (INSTALL_DIR/bin/mquire); the binary
# itself is never something this repo ships or builds from source either.
/bin/

# Same class again - install.py copies the committed pif-companion.apk
# (android_companion/pif-companion.apk, this project's own hand-built
# companion-app SMS/Contacts/Call Log/Calendar extraction relay) here at
# install time. The install-time COPY destination is never itself
# committed - only the real source under android_companion/ is.
/android_companion_tools/

# Gradle build cache/output for android_companion/pif_companion_src - the
# actual source (Java files, manifest, gradle.properties/build.gradle.kts)
# IS committed; the regenerable build cache and compiled output are not,
# matching the standard Android/Gradle .gitignore convention. The final
# built APK itself is committed separately, at android_companion/
# pif-companion.apk (see the note above), not read from this build/ dir.
/android_companion/pif_companion_src/.gradle/
/android_companion/pif_companion_src/app/build/
/android_companion/pif_companion_src/build/

# Runtime hash-list/URL-list storage (Settings > Case & Reporting) - created
# on the target device by routes/settings.py when an examiner uploads/builds
# a Hash Set or URL List (core/config.py's HASH_LISTS_DIR/URL_LISTS_DIR, both
# INSTALL_DIR-relative); never something this repo ships or builds from
# source, same class as /leapp//pysim/ above. Found untracked-but-uncommitted
# on the real deployed station 2026-09-13 - a real gitignore gap, not case
# data, but never should have been committable either.
/hash_lists/
/url_lists/

# Evidence & Data Files (DO NOT PUSH EVIDENCE TO GITHUB)
*.dd
*.raw
*.img
*.aff
*.E01
*.ab
*.log
*_manifest.json
*_manifest.txt
*_report.json
*_report.pdf
/mnt/*
*.bkp

# Runtime secrets - never commit these (install.py/app.py generate them
# on the target device, not in this repo)
runtime_config.json
*.crt
*.key
*.pem
.flask_secret_key
.mount_key

# Per-station operational history/state, not project code - reveals real
# internal network hosts/shares (mount_history.json) or is transient job
# scratch state that can land in the install directory depending on a
# tool's own cwd-relative default (PhotoRec's .ses resume file), a running
# BitLocker/dislocker mount point directory, or pytest's own cache.
mount_history.json
*.ses
.bitlocker_mounts/
.pytest_cache/

# Local Storage / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Real-data test fixtures (2026-09-14). The committed tests use synthetic values
# throughout, on purpose - this repo is public, and a privacy audit found real
# evidence (GPS coordinates at centimetre precision) had been used as a test
# fixture and needed scrubbing from history. Some things are only genuinely
# testable against real tool output though - a real ALEAPP TSV, a real adb
# bugreport, a real SRUM database - so those live here and never leave the
# machine. See tests/conftest.py::local_fixture(): a test that wants one asks
# for it by name and SKIPS if it is absent, so a clean checkout stays green.
tests/fixtures/local/

# Local Claude Code context (not for the repo) - split 2026-09-11 from one oversized CLAUDE.md
# into these five files specifically so the auto-loaded one (CLAUDE.md) stays small; see its own
# "Session continuity" section for what each file is for.
CLAUDE.md
context.md
tasks.md
plan.md
docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md
.claude/

# Source data fetched by tools/bundled_keyword_lists/ when REGENERATING the
# bundled lists (2026-09-15). Its own README tells you to curl these straight
# into that directory, so without this a regeneration run leaves several MB of
# upstream data staged in the repo - the point is to commit the RESULT, not the
# inputs, which are large and go stale. The generated lists themselves
# (bundled_keyword_lists/*.json) ARE committed.
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/gitleaks.toml
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/gitleaks_rules.json
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/creds_selected.json
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/dea_slang.pdf
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/dea_slang.txt
tools/bundled_keyword_lists/dea_themes.json
